    "introduction": "Schroders manages investments for institutions, intermediaries and private clients across public and private markets. Its offerings include equity and bond portfolios, multi-asset strategies, real assets and wealth-management services. Revenue is primarily generated through fees linked to client assets, with some products also earning performance-related income. The business depends on attracting and retaining capital by providing investment expertise, suitable products and service. Market movements change the value of assets under management even without customer inflows or withdrawals. Its broad client base and range of strategies provide different sources of demand, while investment performance, fee competition and distribution relationships influence commercial outcomes.",
